00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:09.310 align:start position:0%
Morsi appeared in public for the first  time since he was deposed on July third  Egyptian state television showed him  arriving at the court with a time delay  and with no sound apparently so the  cheers of his supporters could not be  heard morsi's gesture of defiance was  quickly cut off the former president  seems undaunted despite a rule requiring  white prison garb Morsi unlike his 14  co-defendants wore a suit when the  presiding judge objected scuffles broke  out in the courtroom the trial was  postponed one of morsi's lawyers  described his statement to the court  while the president said that he rejects  the military coup that he rejects the  court and that he rejects the legitimacy  of the prosecutor general Muslim well  thought of a Martha Morsi is charged  with incitement to murder related to  events last December while he was still  president clashes outside the  presidential palace left at least 10  people dead all of them said to be  opponents of the Muslim Brotherhood  prosecutors accuse Morsi of coordinating  the Islamist groups behind the attacks  his defense team has criticized his  treatment  it's not just Morsi supporters who have  doubts about the legality of his ouster  the international community has  expressed concern that the Army's  crackdown on the Muslim Brotherhood  means Egypt could revert to a police  state
 

